description: React, FastAPI, and DuckDB patterns for Loupe
globs: "**/*.{py,sql,ts,tsx}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# React (`web/`)

- Vite + React + TypeScript. Pages in `web/src/pages/`, shared parts in `web/src/components/`
- `web/src/api/client.ts` is the only place that knows the API exists. Relative `/v1` paths
  only — Vite proxies in dev, FastAPI serves `web/dist` in production, so there is no CORS
- No SQL, rule grouping, scoring or bar math in a component. A chart may drop marks it cannot
  fit; it may not average them into new ones
- Charts are the project's own SVG (`web/src/charts/`). An absent session is a dashed labelled
  column, never a zero-height bar — that is why there is no chart library here
- Never spread a series into a call (`Math.max(...points)`): a real VWAP window is >100k points
  and that is a stack overflow. Use `extremes` / `bucketSeries` in `charts/scale.ts`
- Colours come from the tokens in `web/src/theme/`. No gradients, box-shadows, emoji status,
  rainbow colour or KPI-sized type
- Tests: Vitest + Testing Library over a stubbed `fetch`. New envelope keys go in the parity
  list in `web/src/api/schema.test.ts`

# FastAPI

- Routes in `src/loupe/api/`; Pydantic models for request/response
- API owns HTTP; domain logic lives in `quality` / `insights` / `data`
- Return JSON the UI can plot; do not return raw DuckDB relations
- One ingest path (`POST /v1/ingest/batches`). The demo routes reuse its loader rather than
  adding a second pipeline

# DuckDB

- One connection factory; read-heavy analytics in SQL, not Python loops
- Parameterized queries only. Durable files under `data/` (gitignored except fixtures)
- Prefer views for repeated quality/insight queries
